  <SW.Types.PlcStruct ID="0">
    <AttributeList>
      <Interface><Sections xmlns="http://www.siemens.com/automation/Openness/SW/Interface/v5">
  <Section Name="None">
    <Member Name="HopperLevelHigh" Datatype="Bool">
      <AttributeList>
        <BooleanAttribute Name="ExternalAccessible" SystemDefined="true">true</BooleanAttribute>
        <BooleanAttribute Name="ExternalVisible" SystemDefined="true">true</BooleanAttribute>
        <BooleanAttribute Name="ExternalWritable" SystemDefined="true">true</BooleanAttribute>
        <BooleanAttribute Name="SetPoint" SystemDefined="true">false</BooleanAttribute>
      </AttributeList>
      <Comment>
        <MultiLanguageText Lang="en-US">In (FC_ControlMain, from DB_Input.Hopper_Level_High at integration): hopper high-level sensor - the blockage condition this FB supervises for persistence.</MultiLanguageText>
      </Comment>
    </Member>
    <Member Name="PlantRunning" Datatype="Bool">
      <AttributeList>
        <BooleanAttribute Name="ExternalAccessible" SystemDefined="true">true</BooleanAttribute>
        <BooleanAttribute Name="ExternalVisible" SystemDefined="true">true</BooleanAttribute>
        <BooleanAttribute Name="ExternalWritable" SystemDefined="true">true</BooleanAttribute>
        <BooleanAttribute Name="SetPoint" SystemDefined="true">false</BooleanAttribute>
      </AttributeList>
      <Comment>
        <MultiLanguageText Lang="en-US">In (FC_ControlMain, from DB_Input.Shredder_Run_Fwd_FB OR Shredder_Run_Rev_FB): plant-running gate - the persistence window accrues only while the plant actually runs (Q-HBA-04), so a full hopper at standstill never alarms.</MultiLanguageText>
      </Comment>
    </Member>
    <Member Name="FaultReset" Datatype="Bool">
      <AttributeList>
        <BooleanAttribute Name="ExternalAccessible" SystemDefined="true">true</BooleanAttribute>
        <BooleanAttribute Name="ExternalVisible" SystemDefined="true">true</BooleanAttribute>
        <BooleanAttribute Name="ExternalWritable" SystemDefined="true">true</BooleanAttribute>
        <BooleanAttribute Name="SetPoint" SystemDefined="true">false</BooleanAttribute>
      </AttributeList>
      <Comment>
        <MultiLanguageText Lang="en-US">In (FC_ControlMain, from DB_Controls.FaultReset): shared operator reset - clears the latched alarm below. C-115 handshake vocabulary, verbatim across the corpus.</MultiLanguageText>
      </Comment>
    </Member>
    <Member Name="BlockedTimeThreshold" Datatype="Time">
      <AttributeList>
        <BooleanAttribute Name="ExternalAccessible" SystemDefined="true">true</BooleanAttribute>
        <BooleanAttribute Name="ExternalVisible" SystemDefined="true">true</BooleanAttribute>
        <BooleanAttribute Name="ExternalWritable" SystemDefined="true">true</BooleanAttribute>
        <BooleanAttribute Name="SetPoint" SystemDefined="true">false</BooleanAttribute>
      </AttributeList>
      <Comment>
        <MultiLanguageText Lang="en-US">Setting: cumulative high-and-running persistence threshold, seconds (start value T#60S). FB-own tunable per C-307 (not a shared DB_Settings member), commissioning-set as the iDB start value.</MultiLanguageText>
      </Comment>
    </Member>
    <Member Name="ClearDebounceTime" Datatype="Time">
      <AttributeList>
        <BooleanAttribute Name="ExternalAccessible" SystemDefined="true">true</BooleanAttribute>
        <BooleanAttribute Name="ExternalVisible" SystemDefined="true">true</BooleanAttribute>
        <BooleanAttribute Name="ExternalWritable" SystemDefined="true">true</BooleanAttribute>
        <BooleanAttribute Name="SetPoint" SystemDefined="true">false</BooleanAttribute>
      </AttributeList>
      <Comment>
        <MultiLanguageText Lang="en-US">Setting: confirmed-clear filter time, seconds (start value T#2S) - the hopper must read clear continuously this long before the window re-arms, rejecting sensor chatter (Q-HBA-02). FB-own tunable per C-307, commissioning-set.</MultiLanguageText>
      </Comment>
    </Member>
    <Member Name="HopperBlockedAlarm" Datatype="Bool">
      <AttributeList>
        <BooleanAttribute Name="ExternalAccessible" SystemDefined="true">true</BooleanAttribute>
        <BooleanAttribute Name="ExternalVisible" SystemDefined="true">true</BooleanAttribute>
        <BooleanAttribute Name="ExternalWritable" SystemDefined="true">true</BooleanAttribute>
        <BooleanAttribute Name="SetPoint" SystemDefined="true">false</BooleanAttribute>
      </AttributeList>
      <Comment>
        <MultiLanguageText Lang="en-US">Out: latched hopper-blockage alarm (REQ-HBA-001/004). RETAIN - deliberately survives a power cycle (C-124 carve-out), cleared only by FaultReset, like the sequencer's DischargeConveyorTimeoutFault; a blockage needing a human still needs acknowledgement after a restart.</MultiLanguageText>
      </Comment>
    </Member>
    <Member Name="HopperBlockedInhibit" Datatype="Bool">
      <AttributeList>
        <BooleanAttribute Name="ExternalAccessible" SystemDefined="true">true</BooleanAttribute>
        <BooleanAttribute Name="ExternalVisible" SystemDefined="true">true</BooleanAttribute>
        <BooleanAttribute Name="ExternalWritable" SystemDefined="true">true</BooleanAttribute>
        <BooleanAttribute Name="SetPoint" SystemDefined="true">false</BooleanAttribute>
      </AttributeList>
      <Comment>
        <MultiLanguageText Lang="en-US">Out: stop/inhibit demand (Q-HBA-05) - tracks the latched alarm and, being RETAIN, correspondingly persists across a power cycle until acknowledged. The FB writes no shared tag; integration wires this demand to the actual stop separately.</MultiLanguageText>
      </Comment>
    </Member>
  </Section>
</Sections></Interface>
      <IsFailsafeCompliant>false</IsFailsafeCompliant>
      <Name>UDT_HopperBlockageIO</Name>
      <Namespace />
    </AttributeList>
    <ObjectList>
      <MultilingualText ID="1" CompositionName="Comment">
        <ObjectList>
          <MultilingualTextItem ID="2" CompositionName="Items">
            <AttributeList>
              <Culture>en-US</Culture>
              <Text>Caller-visible interface (C-115) for FB_HopperBlockageMonitor. FC_ControlMain writes HopperLevelHigh/PlantRunning/FaultReset in and reads HopperBlockedAlarm/HopperBlockedInhibit out (wiring is a separate integration step). Per the Gate-1 supervisory-monitor exemption (NEW-HBA-07) this pure monitor carries no enable/ready/running vocabulary stubs. BlockedTimeThreshold/ClearDebounceTime are this instance's own tunables (C-307), commissioning defaults set as the iDB start values.</Text>
            </AttributeList>
          </MultilingualTextItem>
        </ObjectList>
      </MultilingualText>
